# Paperu environment variables
#
# The Paperu foundation does NOT require any environment variables
# to build, run, or test. This file documents the placeholders for
# future secrets that the release pipeline will use when code-signing
# and licensing are wired in.
#
# Do NOT commit real secrets to this file. Do NOT commit a real
# `.env` file. This is a `.env.example`; real values live in CI
# secrets (or a developer's local `.env` that is gitignored).
#
# See:
#   - docs/releases/workflow.md   (signing plan)
#   - docs/decisions/0009-no-telemetry.md   (no telemetry by default)
#   - docs/decisions/0010-commercial-licensing-boundary.md
#       (no production keys are committed)

# ── Foundation: no environment variables required ─────────────────
#
# The foundation builds and runs without any of the variables below.
# They are documented as placeholders so that, when a feature needs
# them, the secret name and shape are already agreed.
#
# To run the foundation:
#   pnpm install
#   pnpm dev              # frontend dev server (Vite)
#   pnpm dev:tauri        # full Tauri dev (Windows / Linux GTK)
#   pnpm check            # full validation gate (or scripts/check.sh)
#
# No environment variable is required for any of these.


# ── Code-signing (Windows release artifact) ───────────────────────
#
# Status: NOT YET ACTIVE. No certificate is in the repository today.
# See docs/releases/workflow.md for the full signing plan.
#
# When a certificate is procured, these secrets are set in CI (or
# in a developer's local, gitignored `.env` for local signing tests).
# They are NEVER committed to the repository.

# Windows Authenticode certificate (base64-encoded PFX), used by
# signtool to sign the installer and inner binaries.
# WINDOWS_SIGNING_CERTIFICATE=

# Password for the Windows signing certificate.
# WINDOWS_SIGNING_PASSWORD=


# ── Tauri updater signature ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# Status: NOT YET ACTIVE. The Tauri updater is disabled
# (tauri.conf.json: createUpdaterArtifacts: false).
# See docs/releases/workflow.md for the full updater plan.
#
# When the updater is enabled, these secrets are set in CI. The
# public key is embedded in tauri.conf.json (NOT a secret). The
# private key and its password are secrets and are NEVER committed.

# Tauri updater signing private key (PEM). Used to sign the updater
# artifact (.msi.zip or similar) so the running Paperu can verify
# it against the embedded public key.
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Password for the Tauri updater signing private key.
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=


# ── Licensing (future) ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Status: NOT YET ACTIVE. The desktop client never trusts itself for
# payment verification. See docs/decisions/0010-commercial-licensing-boundary.md
# and docs/architecture/licensing.md.
#
# When the activation flow lands:
#   - The Razorpay integration lives SERVER-SIDE. No Razorpay keys
#     are in this repository, ever.
#   - The desktop client only ever holds a licence key (an opaque
#     string the user pastes) and a signed entitlement blob (a
#     signed view the server returns).
#   - The entitlement verification public key is embedded in the
#     desktop binary at build time. It is NOT a secret.
#   - The corresponding private key (which signs entitlement blobs)
#     lives on the entitlement server, NEVER in this repository.
#
# No PAPERU_LICENCE_* or PAPERU_RAZORPAY_* variables are documented
# here because they do not belong in the desktop codebase.


# ── Telemetry ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Status: PROHIBITED BY DEFAULT. No telemetry, no analytics, no
# crash uploading. See docs/decisions/0009-no-telemetry.md.
#
# There is no TELEMETRY_* variable and there will not be one without
# a deliberate architecture decision. If a future opt-in telemetry
# feature is added, it will:
#   - default to OFF (TELEMETRY_DEFAULT_ON = false in src/security/mod.rs)
#   - require an ADR (docs/decisions/)
#   - be opt-in by the user, off by default
#   - never upload file contents or secrets


# ── Local development overrides ───────────────────────────────────
#
# The foundation does not read any of these. They are documented as
# possible future local-dev conveniences; none are required today.

# Override the app data directory for local testing (default:
# %LOCALAPPDATA%/app.paperu.desktop on Windows). Useful for testing
# first-launch behaviour against a clean directory.
# PAPERU_APP_DATA_DIR=

# Override the log level for the structured tracing sink (default:
# info). One of: error, warn, info, debug, trace.
# PAPERU_LOG_LEVEL=

# Override the temp workspace root for testing (default: %TEMP%/paperu
# on Windows). Useful for inspecting temp outputs without disturbing
# the real workspace.
# PAPERU_TEMP_DIR=
